-- Content quality repair (2026-09-30).
--
-- Fixes three defects that made shipped content misleading:
--   * the 940 auto-generated "Practice — <topic>" questions asked the same
--     question ten times per quiz, offered options lifted from *other* topics'
--     notes, and put the correct answer at position B in 488 of 940 cases
--     (never at A) — so always picking B scored over 50%. Each one is rebuilt
--     from its own topic's notes: a positive form ("which statement is from the
--     X notes?") plus a NOT form once that topic's facts run out, so ten unique
--     items need no invented content and never repeat the same key. Options must
--     be complete statements, so a section heading or half-written formula cannot
--     appear as an answer.
--   * the curated questions had the correct answer at position A 34% of the time.
--   * every flashcard in 100 decks was a restatement of the topic title; they are
--     now term/definition pairs taken from the notes.
--
-- Also backfills past_papers.level / subject_slug from the linked topic: both
-- were NULL on all 378 rows, and the discovery filter reads those columns.
--
-- Generated by .freebuff/gen-content-fix.cjs. Content updates only, no schema
-- change. questions.options is jsonb, hence the to_jsonb() wrappers.

begin;

