update public.questions set question_text = $cm$From the "Functions" notes, which statement appears?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Solve by sketching. For x² − 5x + 4 < 0, factorise: (x − 1)(x − 4) < 0, and the curve is below the axis between the roots, so 1 < x < 4$cm$::text, $cm$Use the symmetry of the graphs. For sin x = 1/2 in 0 ≤ x ≤ 2π: the acute answer is π/6, and the second solution is π − π/6 = 5π/6$cm$::text, $cm$If not, restrict the domain (e.g. f(x) = x² for x ≥ 0 has f⁻¹(x) = √x). Graphically, y = f⁻¹(x) is the reflection of y = f(x) in the line y = x, and t$cm$::text, $cm$A quadratic has the form ax² + bx + c with a ≠ 0. Master three tools: completing the square, the discriminant, and inequalities$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 2, explanation = $cm$From the Functions study notes: “If not, restrict the domain (e.g. f(x) = x² for x ≥ 0 has f⁻¹(x) = √x). Graphically, y = f⁻¹(x) is the reflection of y = f(x) in the line y = x, and t”.$cm$ where id = '76a4b169-42bd-4f27-ae2e-7b9e592623d1';
