update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which of these is covered by the "Measurement & Units" study notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Heating → particles vibrate more → solids expand slightly (gases expand most). Applications: bimetallic strip (fire alarm/thermostat), gaps in bridges$cm$::text, $cm$Cambridge IGCSE 0625 (2026–2028): 1.1 lengths & volumes; 1.2 density; 1.3 forces & motion context (measurements) — plus measurement techniques, SI uni$cm$::text, $cm$v = fλ. Transverse (oscillation ⊥ travel — light, water, S-waves) vs longitudinal (parallel — sound, P-waves). Amplitude, wavelength, frequency f = 1/$cm$::text, $cm$P = VI = I²R = V²/R; E = VIt. Fuse rating just above normal current; earth wire, double insulation, circuit breakers (trip quickly, resettable)$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 1, explanation = $cm$From the Measurement & Units study notes: “Cambridge IGCSE 0625 (2026–2028): 1.1 lengths & volumes; 1.2 density; 1.3 forces & motion context (measurements) — plus measurement techniques, SI uni”.$cm$ where id = '2c7b8a46-fb48-4cad-9e28-4490388860e0';
