update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which statement belongs to the "Circular Motion and SHM" notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Diffraction grating: d sin θ = nλ — resolution of spectra$cm$::text, $cm$Young's double slit: x = λD/a — evidence light is a wave$cm$::text, $cm$Wien: λ_max T = 2.9 × 10⁻³ m K — hotter stars are bluer$cm$::text, $cm$Angular speed ω = 2π/T; v = ωr; a = ω²r = v²/r; F = mv²/r toward the centre$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 3, explanation = $cm$From the Circular Motion and SHM study notes: “Angular speed ω = 2π/T; v = ωr; a = ω²r = v²/r; F = mv²/r toward the centre”.$cm$ where id = '17b88eab-e9e2-405b-9729-bdaaa92b5ae6';
update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which statement is from the "Circular Motion and SHM" study notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Acceleration is proportional to displacement and opposite: a = −ω²x$cm$::text, $cm$F = BIL sin θ (Fleming's left hand: field-index, current-first-finger, force-thumb)$cm$::text, $cm$F = q₁q₂/(4πε₀r²). Field strength E = F/q (N C⁻¹); for a point charge E = q/(4πε₀r²)$cm$::text, $cm$Galaxies recede with v = Hd, H₀ ≈ 2.2 × 10⁻¹⁸ s⁻¹. Redshift z = Δλ/λ ≈ v/c for small z$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 0, explanation = $cm$From the Circular Motion and SHM study notes: “Acceleration is proportional to displacement and opposite: a = −ω²x”.$cm$ where id = 'd802ba42-7429-448f-803b-f0c64db71f1c';
update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which of these is covered by the "Circular Motion and SHM" study notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Luminosity L is total power radiated (W). Intensity at distance d: I = L/(4πd²) — the key to distances$cm$::text, $cm$Solutions: x = x₀ sin ωt (start at centre) or x = x₀ cos ωt (start at extreme), with ω = 2πf$cm$::text, $cm$Atoms absorb/emit photons matching level gaps: hf = E₁ − E₂. Emission lines are bright; absorption dark$cm$::text, $cm$Nuclear densities are enormous (~10¹⁷ kg m⁻³) — nearly all mass in a tiny volume$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 1, explanation = $cm$From the Circular Motion and SHM study notes: “Solutions: x = x₀ sin ωt (start at centre) or x = x₀ cos ωt (start at extreme), with ω = 2πf”.$cm$ where id = '8c62fd10-39b5-4be4-9850-fe141f4e57aa';
update public.questions set question_text = $cm$From the "Circular Motion and SHM" notes, which statement appears?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Pressure law: p/T = constant (V fixed)$cm$::text, $cm$Age estimate: t ≈ 1/H₀ ≈ 14 billion years$cm$::text, $cm$a_max = ω²x₀ at the extremes$cm$::text, $cm$Between parallel plates: E = V/d, constant$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 2, explanation = $cm$From the Circular Motion and SHM study notes: “a_max = ω²x₀ at the extremes”.$cm$ where id = '24101685-4bbe-478a-a824-da67f60adfd1';
update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which statement belongs to the "Circular Motion and SHM" notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Faraday: induced EMF = rate of flux cutting = N dΦ/dt. Lenz: induced effects oppose the change (negative sign)$cm$::text, $cm$Noise-cancelling headphones: destructive interference of antiphase sound$cm$::text, $cm$Long straight wire: B = μ₀I/(2πr), circling by the right-hand grip rule$cm$::text, $cm$E = ½mω²x₀² total (constant), exchanged between KE (max at centre) and PE (max at extremes)$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 3, explanation = $cm$From the Circular Motion and SHM study notes: “E = ½mω²x₀² total (constant), exchanged between KE (max at centre) and PE (max at extremes)”.$cm$ where id = 'aeaa7902-5886-4926-b714-169057cb1147';
update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which statement is from the "Circular Motion and SHM" study notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Damping removes energy: light damping → slow decay; critical → fastest return without oscillation$cm$::text, $cm$de Broglie: λ = h/p = h/(mv). Electrons diffract like waves — electron microscopes exploit short electron wavelengths$cm$::text, $cm$Half-life: time for half the nuclei to decay. N = N₀ e^(−λt), λ = ln 2 / t½$cm$::text, $cm$A string fixed at both ends: f₁ = v/2L, then 2f₁, 3f₁… Closed pipes resonate at odd multiples; open pipes at all multiples$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 0, explanation = $cm$From the Circular Motion and SHM study notes: “Damping removes energy: light damping → slow decay; critical → fastest return without oscillation”.$cm$ where id = 'f32b604e-1d05-4512-ba2c-03847203d9f9';
update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which of these is covered by the "Circular Motion and SHM" study notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Exponential: V = V₀ e^(−t/RC). Time constant RC: after one RC, V falls to 37%. Half-life t½ = 0.69 RC$cm$::text, $cm$Resonance: driving at the natural frequency gives maximum amplitude (microwave ovens, swing pushing, bridge disasters)$cm$::text, $cm$E = mc². Mass difference Δm in nuclear reactions becomes energy; binding energy = energy released assembling the nucleus. 1 u ≈ 931 MeV$cm$::text, $cm$Standard candles (Cepheid variables, Type Ia supernovae) have known L, so measuring I gives d$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 1, explanation = $cm$From the Circular Motion and SHM study notes: “Resonance: driving at the natural frequency gives maximum amplitude (microwave ovens, swing pushing, bridge disasters)”.$cm$ where id = '27598c8b-28c4-4e22-a784-12a8d4af446f';
update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which statement is missing from the "Circular Motion and SHM" notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Angular speed ω = 2π/T; v = ωr; a = ω²r = v²/r; F = mv²/r toward the centre$cm$::text, $cm$Acceleration is proportional to displacement and opposite: a = −ω²x$cm$::text, $cm$V = W/q, scalar; E = −dV/dr. Potential energy of q at V is qV$cm$::text, $cm$Solutions: x = x₀ sin ωt (start at centre) or x = x₀ cos ωt (start at extreme), with ω = 2πf$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 2, explanation = $cm$The other three are all in the Circular Motion and SHM study notes; this one is not.$cm$ where id = '8b6ac86c-5cb8-4412-a521-b2f87995ec89';
update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which of these is NOT part of the "Circular Motion and SHM" notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$Acceleration is proportional to displacement and opposite: a = −ω²x$cm$::text, $cm$Solutions: x = x₀ sin ωt (start at centre) or x = x₀ cos ωt (start at extreme), with ω = 2πf$cm$::text, $cm$a_max = ω²x₀ at the extremes$cm$::text, $cm$Diffraction grating: d sin θ = nλ — resolution of spectra$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 3, explanation = $cm$The other three are all in the Circular Motion and SHM study notes; this one is not.$cm$ where id = 'eed5c8e9-da91-4562-9da0-72f4cfb9f2a1';
