update public.questions set question_text = $cm$Which of these is covered by the "Magnetic Fields and Electromagnetism" study notes?$cm$, options = to_jsonb(array[$cm$E = mc². Mass difference Δm in nuclear reactions becomes energy; binding energy = energy released assembling the nucleus. 1 u ≈ 931 MeV$cm$::text, $cm$F = BQv sin θ, always perpendicular to v → circular paths: r = mv/(BQ) (basis of cyclotrons and mass spectrometers)$cm$::text, $cm$Standard candles (Cepheid variables, Type Ia supernovae) have known L, so measuring I gives d$cm$::text, $cm$Solutions: x = x₀ sin ωt (start at centre) or x = x₀ cos ωt (start at extreme), with ω = 2πf$cm$::text]::text[]), correct_option = 1, explanation = $cm$From the Magnetic Fields and Electromagnetism study notes: “F = BQv sin θ, always perpendicular to v → circular paths: r = mv/(BQ) (basis of cyclotrons and mass spectrometers)”.$cm$ where id = '2f158cc5-6618-4ea0-bf43-f0aa7bf4c1fa';
